<!--Post: 5390--><!--Time: 1107101928-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5390"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 8:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->March 19, 2004 Communication #1 <BR>A letter arrives at the Wichita Eagle containing a single sheet of paper. The paper is a photocopy of Vicki Wegerle&#39;s driver&#39;s license and three pictures of the crime scene that apparently were taken by the killer.  <BR> <BR>May 5, 2004 Communication #2  <BR>KAKE- TV receives a second letter from BTK. The letter contained a word search puzzle with words pertaining to BTK&#39;s mo, and I.D. The letter also contained photocopies of two id cards, one for a Southwestern Bell worker and another for a former employee of the Wichita schools.  <BR> <BR>June 1 &#40;?&#41;, 2004 Communication #3  <BR>Police received a third letter from BTK. They say it contained writings about the Otero murders.  <BR> <BR>July 17, 2004 Communication #4 <BR>BTK leaves a letter in the drop off box of the main branch of the Wichita Public Library. Police say a worker there found the letter and called police.  <BR> <BR>October 21, 2004 Communication #5  <BR>A letter was found at the UPS drop box in an office complex at the Omni Center, 250 North Kansas St. Police say it contained some biographical information on BTK.   <BR> <BR>December 13, 2004  Communication #6 <BR>A package was left in Murdock Park. A local citizen was walking through the park when he found the plastic bag. Police say inside they found what appears to be the driver&#39;s license of Nancy Fox.   <BR> <BR>January 26, 2005 Communication #7  <BR>BTK&#39;s 7th message is not found until instructions are sent to KAKE in Communication #8. Communication #8 asked if #7 had been located. Working off of instructions on the postcard, police recovered the seventh package on January 26th. They have not revealed to the public what the packaged contained or where it was recovered. <BR> <BR>January 25, 2004 Communication #8 <BR>KAKE received a postcard that claimed to be &#34;Communication #8&#34;.  A crew went to the scene and found, a Post Toasties Corn Flakes box, weighted with a brick on top, leaning against a road sign.  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5390-->
<!--Post: 5453--><!--Time: 1107127051-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5453"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 3:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Essevi -- Nice synopsis of the communications.  <BR> <BR>It is curious to me that Communication #7 was somehow overlooked.  <BR> <BR>That brings me to another question. Wasn&#39;t there a phone call to a convenience store directing them to a drop - or am I doing the &#34;memory filling&#34; trick?  Or perhaps that was in one of his older communications? <BR> <BR>I thought I read it here, but perhaps I&#39;m wrong.  <BR> <BR>Anyway, if there was truly a call to a store -- do we have any information as to the phone it was called in from?  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5453-->
<!--Post: 5454--><!--Time: 1107129141-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5454"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 3:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That would be the Murdock Park, drop #6 above...WPD would have gotten a phone dump of the QT phone records...to my knowledge they have not said where that phone call came from...good point... <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5454-->
<!--Post: 5746--><!--Time: 1107319183-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5746"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 8:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Has anyone seen the close-up pics of the cereal box? Anyone think the streamers are in celebration of a birthday? <BR>Also, is it really possible to handle that much packing tape, streamers, and paper without leaving physical evidence?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5746-->
<!--Post: 5751--><!--Time: 1107325883-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5751"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 10:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s possible, but would probably be a pain, to handle all that paper and paper-related material and not leave prints. However, BTK is cocky and while it may be unlikely perhaps he forgot about <a href="http://www.geocities.com/cfpdlab/ninhydri.htm" target="_blank"> Ninhydrin</a>. <BR> <BR>Maybe the streamers were used to make the location of the cereal box more visible? Just a guess.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5751-->
